# War Card Game

A simple Java-based version of the classic card game **War**.

This project is designed as a two-person programming project, where both developers can work together using **VS Code Live Share** or GitHub. The goal is to practise object-oriented programming, class design, queues, game logic, and clean project structure.

---

## Project Idea

War is a two-player card game.

The deck is shuffled and split evenly between two players. Each round, both players draw their top card. The player with the higher card wins the round and takes both cards.

If both cards have the same value, a **war** happens. During war, both players place cards face down, then flip another card. The higher card wins the full pile.

---

## Example Game Output

```text
================================
          WAR CARD GAME
================================

Round 1

Stephen plays: 10 of Hearts
Brother plays: 6 of Clubs

Stephen wins the round!

Stephen cards: 27
Brother cards: 25
```

War example:

```text
Round 8

Stephen plays: Jack of Spades
Brother plays: Jack of Diamonds

WAR!

Stephen places 3 cards face down.
Brother places 3 cards face down.

Stephen war card: 8 of Hearts
Brother war card: Queen of Clubs

Brother wins the war!

Stephen cards: 20
Brother cards: 32
```

