## Suggested Features

### Basic Version

```text
- Create a 52-card deck
- Shuffle the deck
- Create two players
- Deal 26 cards to each player
- Play rounds
- Compare card values
- Give won cards to the round winner
- Detect when a player has no cards
- Print the winner
```

### Intermediate Version

```text
- Add proper war logic
- Add player names
- Add round counter
- Add card count after each round
- Add "Press Enter to continue"
- Improve terminal display
```

### Advanced Version

```text
- Add ASCII card art
- Add save/load game
- Add game statistics
- Add best-of-three mode
- Add menu system
- Add LAN multiplayer later
```

---

## Responsibility Split

This project is good for two people because the work can be split clearly.

### Developer 1

```text
- Card class
- Deck class
- Shuffle logic
- Deal logic
```

### Developer 2

```text
- Player class
- Queue/card hand logic
- playRound()
- handleWar()
```

### Both Developers

```text
- Main menu
- Testing
- Better terminal output
- Bug fixing
- Extra features
```

---

## Key Design Decision

The most important design choice is:

```text
Player hand = Queue<Card>
```

This is because War works like a queue:

```text
Draw from the front
Add won cards to the back
```

That makes `Queue<Card>` the correct data structure for each player's hand.

---

## Final Mental Model

```text
Card   = one playing card
Deck   = creates and shuffles all cards
Player = owns a queue of cards
Game   = controls the rules and decides who wins
```
